        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI think I understand your suggestion (clear query after evaluating item), but at the moment not sure if this is a better behavior. I'll think about it a bit more.\r\n\r\n> This is especially notable when enabling the 'evaluate_single' option. When multiple windows have been opened using queries, every backspace triggers a reopening of the selected item.\r\n\r\nNow this is more interesting. I am having trouble seeing such a scenario in real life. `evaluate_single` should lead to item evaluation immediately after it becomes single. If after that your return to the same Starter buffer and type one backspace, this, in theory, should lead to at least two items. Would you mind sharing (as minimal as you can) `config` and exact steps to reproduce this?",
