            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This is the best I could \r\n```lua\r\nvim.cmd [[packadd packer.nvim]]\r\n\r\nrequire('packer').startup(function()\r\n    -- Packer can manage itself\r\n    use 'wbthomason/packer.nvim'\r\n\r\n    use({ 'echasnovski/mini.nvim' })\r\n    use {\r\n        'nvim-telescope/telescope.nvim',\r\n        requires = { {'nvim-lua/plenary.nvim'} }\r\n    }\r\nend)\r\n\r\nrequire('telescope').setup()\r\nlocal starter = require('mini.starter')\r\n\r\nstarter.setup({\r\n    items = {\r\n        function()\r\n            return {\r\n                { name = 'Find', action = 'Telescope find_files', section = 'Workspace' },\r\n                { name = 'Grep', action = 'Telescope live_grep', section = 'Workspace' },\r\n                { name = 'Recent', action = 'Telescope oldfiles', section = 'Global' },\r\n            }\r\n        end\r\n    },\r\n    content_hooks = {\r\n        starter.gen_hook.adding_bullet(),\r\n        starter.gen_hook.aligning('center', 'center'),\r\n    },\r\n    query_updaters = [[abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_-.]],\r\n    footer = '',\r\n    evaluate_single = true\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nActions to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Run `nvim`\r\n2. Press 'g' to open telescope grep  \r\n3. Press esc twice to close popup\r\n4. Press 'r' as if you would like to open recents\r\n5. Grep popup opens again\r\n6. Be confused\r\n7. Close popup and try to press backspace to clear query\r\n8. Grep popup open again\r\n9. Again close popup and press backspace\r\n10. Now press 'r' and Telescope with recent files will open",
