        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "That was very clear, thanks! Especially step 6 was very crucial :)\r\n\r\nI don't think I like the idea of auto clearing the query at item execution. What I ended up implementing in current `main` (be sure to update plugin) is a user-facing `MiniStarter.set_query()` function. If called without arguments, it resets query. By default it is also mapped to `<Esc>`, so you can clear query without using `<BS>`.\r\n\r\nTo solve your particular problem, you can do at least two things:\r\n- Manually update all \"non-Starter-closing\" actions to first call `lua MiniStarter.set_query('')`. So to be like `silent lua MiniStarter.set_query(''); vim.cmd('Telescope find_files')`.\r\n- Add autocommand `au BufEnter Starter silent lua MiniStarter.set_query('')`. This will reset query every time you re-enter the Starter buffer. Although not *exactly* the solution to your problem, I think this might be a good compromise for you.\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your issue?",
