        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "As for my opinion about clearing the query, it is mainly based two points:\r\n- 'mini.starter' initially is designed to serve as a start screen allowing user to have a moment to decide what to do next (open file, open session, etc.). It is meant to disappear after doing that next thing (not obligated to, but is a main design). So having to do something extra before any execution seems to be an unnecessary complication.\r\n- Your use case with typo and `evaluate_single` is quite reasonable, but it involved typing only single letter. There are scenarios, when typing several letters are needed in order to single out one item. In this case it will require more work from user to recreate query if it will have been cleared.",
